3:Learned LSA distils the indexer while the language model is frozen, and this is how to run that.
22:### On GLM-5.3-Flash
34:    $LSA_ROOT/models/maps/glm53_flash__long-16k-1M-heavy-key-and-query-d2048.pt
52:The model does not fit one card, so GLM distils from a cache rather than online: one extraction pass, then any number of runs.
57:The attention input `x` is a research option: `model_dim` dims a token, with no heads to regroup and no rotary to undo.
64:### On Qwen3.8-27B - the teacher online
66:A cache of `x` for Qwen3.8-27B over the heavy mix would be some 60 TiB, so its run reads none: `data.teacher` names the extraction config, and the frozen model reads the documents the run draws as it trains.
74:The maps train on the first card and a copy of the model reads documents on each of the others, every layer of a document at once, into the same pool a cache feeds.
83:`--nodes n` spreads the teacher rather than the layers: the trainer stays on the first node's first card, and every other card of every node holds a copy of the model.
97:The model card carries the rotation the model is served under - YaRN to 10M as `rope_parameters` - and every load applies it, so the targets are the attention the served model pays.
100:### The model is frozen
102:One pass per document extracts what the objective and the metrics need - the key and query at every position (the attention input `x` for the research option), and the attention the teacher actually paid to the keys a whole-bucket read may see - so a run loads in minutes rather than holding a model for the whole of training.
103:The extraction drives the model through its [adapter](adapters.md), so a checkpoint an adapter exists for is one this extracts from.
108:What comes out is the indexer an injected checkpoint carries, not a trained language model.
123:A run is three blocks and nothing else: `model` is what is trained - the model card, the indexer and the learned space - `data` is which targets it reads and which of their documents train and score it, and `run` is how - the name, the output, the objective, the optimiser, the reports and wandb.
125:Each model's `base.yaml` sets it once, `${root:training/distillation/<model card>}` under the shared root, the same directory names `configs/training/distillation` has, along with `model.name`, and every run in that directory names `base` first in its `defaults`.
161:    'model.space.init=${root:training/distillation/glm53_flash/long_16k_1m_heavy_key_and_query_d2048/maps.pt}'
165:Rescoring scores maps that are already trained, named by `model.space.init`, over a grid of reads, with no gradient and no training document loaded.
176:`model.space.init` names the exported map, and the picks are the `_native.pt` sidecars `lsa distill native-picks` writes.
224:lsa distill inject --model glm53_flash --maps "$LSA_ROOT/training/distillation/glm53_flash/<run>/maps.pt" \
