272:A tokenized card says which sources and which tokenizer, and how long a row is, and its manifest beside the bytes says how wide the vocabulary is and how many rows each source gave; a model card says which family builds the checkpoint, which flavour the published one is, and where its rotation sits.
278:## Native - a model trained under the multi-resolution attention
286:One file is one arm: `base.yaml` holds the model from random initialisation, the corpus and the schedule, and each arm names it and sets `attention`.
304:`evaluate` scores a checkpoint's weights on the held-out set, the default `--suite held-out`, with no optimiser and no training data, under the attention the file and its overrides name, so a trained model can be read with the summaries off.
317:The RULER files are NVIDIA's generators' output sized by the model's own tokenizer, prepared into a root of their own once with `lsa data prepare ruler --root <root> --tokenizer <tokenizer snapshot> --tasks ... --lengths 4096 8192 16384 32768 --samples 100`, and the datasets of the core tasks are fetched once on the login node into the shared hub cache.
