## Appendix A Attention Sparsity

To test how many keys a query needs to keep accuracy, we let each query of Qwen-3.8-27B attend only to the sink, the window and its true top-kk keys (Figure [8](#A0.F8 "Figure 8")). At 128k tokens, Top-kk Oracle Attention keeps 98% of the RULER accuracy of Full Attention down to k\=512k=512, while each query attends to 0.8% of the keys. Single-needle retrieval holds down to k\=16k=16, while MultiKey 2, MultiKey 3 and CWE fall first in accuracy. Therefore, sparse attention loses little if it finds the most relevant keys, which is what LSA is designed to do without scoring every key.

